Third-party copyright notices for the acir package
==================================================

acir is verified against, and parts of its numerical core derive from, the
reference MATLAB implementation ACI_code (repository
https://github.com/marandmath/ACI_code, commit
733c49fc5a36a5dad857608ef550a8f836466144, as pinned by the oracle manifest in
tests/testthat/fixtures/oracles/oracle-manifest.yml), whose MIT licence notice
is reproduced in full below. The composite Simpson quadrature used by acir is
an independent R implementation of a documented rule: ACI_code vendors simps.m
by Damien Garcia under a BSD 2-clause licence, that file is executed only in
the reference MATLAB environment when the comparison fixtures are generated and
was never ported into this package, so no simps.m notice is required here.

ACI_code is not redistributed with this package.


